{"raw": {"https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2789": {"title": "Data Specialist II", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Data Specialist II Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Data Specialist II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Position Details Position Information Position Title Data Specialist II Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division University President Department Institutional Effectiveness Job Location Remote/Hybrid Option Position Summary The Data Specialist II at Doane University is responsible for supporting the institution\u2019s data-driven decision-making processes by providing actionable insights through data analysis, data governance, and reporting. This role requires a combination of strategic thinking and hands-on technical expertise in analytics tools. The position plays a critical role in advancing the institution\u2019s data maturity model by developing data models, creating reports, and ensuring data quality across systems, especially in Salesforce. The position will work closely with institutional leadership to provide data insights that support operational and business changes, while also alleviating reporting burdens from database administrators. This position is funded by a Title III Strengthening Institutions Program Grant and offers a unique opportunity to impact how we support students from enrollment through graduation and into their careers. Given the nature of grant funding, employment is contingent on the continued availability of external funding. View full position description Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. FLSA Salaried (Exempt) Salary $85,000 Minimum Required Qualifications A bachelor\u2019s degree/equivalent experience will be considered, and 3+ years of experience in data analytics, reporting, or business intelligence. Experience must include: Data Analysis and Manipulation, Data Visualization and Business Intelligence (Power BI or Tableau), Statistical Analysis and Predictive Modeling, Data Warehousing and Big Data (Databricks or other tool), Data Integration, ETL , Customer Relationship Management ( CRM ) Analytics, Reporting and Automation Salesforce CRM or similar tools. The successful candidate must be able to demonstrate: Strong skills in data analysis, statistics, and business intelligence tools. Ability to translate complex data into clear insights and actionable recommendations. Proficiency in developing and maintaining dashboards and data models. Strong written and verbal communication skills for storytelling with data. Ability to work collaboratively across departments and train staff on data tools. Familiarity with data privacy and security standards. Preferred Qualifications A master\u2019s degree/equivalent experience will be considered. Experience in higher education or a similar institutional environment. Experience with advanced statistical analysis and predictive modeling. Experience with student retention tools (Salesforce CRM ) is a plus. Experience with cloud-based data platforms. Familiarity with SQL and database query languages. Knowledge of institutional data governance frameworks and practices. Familiarity with Power BI and Databricks Required Licenses/Certifications Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Normal business hours Evenings and weekends as necessary (i.e., emergencies) Remote option available Travel to campuses as necessary for projects and collaborations Travel Required No Physical Requirements Sedentary work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF209 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date 10/28/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2780 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Is the salary or salary range listed in the job posting acceptable to you? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2788": {"title": "Employer Relations Coordinator", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Employer Relations Coordinator Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Employer Relations Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Position Details Position Information Position Title Employer Relations Coordinator Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division Student Affairs Department Career, Leadership, and Service Job Location Remote/Hybrid Option Position Summary The Employer Relations Coordinator for CLS will work as a member of the Career, Leadership & Service staff, focusing on building and maintaining relationships with external employers and organizations. Additionally, this role will continue to develop the strategies necessary to engage outside partners as they seek to recruit and connect with all Doane students and alumni. This individual will be the primary contact for employers and organizations seeking to connect with CLS and will work with campus partners to help connect opportunities. This is a hybrid position; the individual will work remotely and be located in the Lincoln or Omaha metro area to increase employer relations for Doane. This position is funded by a Title III Strengthening Institutions Program Grant and offers a unique opportunity to impact how we support students from enrollment through graduation and into their careers. Given the nature of grant funding, employment is contingent on the continued availability of external funding. View full job description Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. FLSA Salaried (Exempt) Salary $55,000 Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree and 2+ years of professional experience in employer relations, university career services, corporate talent acquisition/recruiting, alumni relations, business development, sales, or related relationship-management fields. The successful applicant must demonstrate: Excellent interpersonal, communication, organizational, relationship-building, and time-management skills. Ability to work effectively in a team environment is essential. Attention to detail, a high level of accuracy, the ability to learn extensive requirements, policies, and procedures, and the use of various technology platforms are necessary. The ability to network and connect with many different types of people and build relationships back to the institution. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Human Resources, Business Administration, Communication, or a related field. Experience utilizing career services platforms (e.g., Handshake, 12Twenty, Simplicity) and CRM systems (e.g., Salesforce). Demonstrated success in establishing corporate/community partnerships and building pipeline initiatives from inception to execution. Required Licenses/Certifications Valid Nebraska driver\u2019s license and driving record acceptable to the college\u2019s automobile insurance provider Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Full-time, standard business hours (Monday\u2013Friday, 40 hours/week) with occasional evenings and weekends required for networking events, career fairs, and alumni activities. Hybrid position based in the Lincoln or Omaha metro area, combining remote flexibility with regular campus visits, partner site visits, and community networking events. Regular travel within Nebraska/Midwest for employer site visits, recruitment events, and conferences. Travel Required Yes Physical Requirements Sedentary work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF208 Desired Start Date 12/01/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date 11/04/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2785 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Is the salary or salary range listed in the job posting acceptable to you? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2787": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - Communications", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Adjunct Faculty - Communications Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Adjunct Faculty - Communications Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of unofficial transcripts of all graduate work. Official transcripts will be required as a condition of employment. Position Details Position Information Position Title Adjunct Faculty - Communications Unit School of Communication, English, History, and Spanish Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Description of Work Doane University, a nationally recognized liberal arts university in Nebraska, invites applications for Adjunct Faculty in the School of Communication, English, History, and Spanish. Courses will be taught during the Spring Semester 2027. CMS 210 \u2013 Public Speaking \u2013 in person in Crete, NE This course focuses on the development of effective public speaking skills. Students completing this course will understand audience analysis, exigency analysis, and critical analysis of content. CMS 495 \u2013 Strategic Communication Capstone (3) \u2013 prefer in person in Crete; may consider synchronous online for well-qualified applicants. This is the capstone course for the Strategic Communication major. Students and the instructor will work together to devise a research project or campaign that synthesizes students\u2019 unique journey through their coursework, highlights strengths, firms up weaknesses, and results in a piece of scholarship of application, integration, or discovery. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. Minimum Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Communication or related field. A commitment to teaching in an undergraduate liberal arts university is expected from strong candidates. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. or Advanced ABD in Communication or a related field Required Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel Required No Background Check Required Yes Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC069 Desired Start Date 01/11/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of unofficial transcripts of all graduate work. Official transcripts will be required as a condition of employment. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2774 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Philosophy Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2783": {"title": "Project Manager", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Project Manager Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Project Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Position Details Position Information Position Title Project Manager Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division Enrollment Management Department Office of Strategic Marketing Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary Serving a key role in the Office of Strategic Marketing ( OSM ) operations, the Project Manager is responsible for overseeing projects from initial project scope until final deliverable and ensuring that projects meet client expectations and are completed on time. The Project Manager actively engages in client outreach to understand immediate and future needs. This position is responsible for keeping projects moving forward to completion both internally and externally. The position will maintain open and complete communication with OSM colleagues, on-campus partners, and vendors regarding project status. This includes managing project revisions and feedback and overseeing the accuracy of edits to ensure all rounds of revisions meet the expectations of our on-campus partners. This position will proactively coordinate and schedule meetings with clear outcomes when necessary. The Project Manager will be responsible for sending out project bids, requesting quotes, processing invoices, and other departmental billing responsibilities. The Project Manager will also maintain physical and digital archives of projects, estimates, print materials, and invoices. View full job description Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Following USCIS regulations, successful applicants must be legally able to accept work in the United States. Doane is unable to sponsor applicants for work visas. FLSA Salaried (Exempt) Salary Minimum $55,000/year Minimum Required Qualifications A bachelor\u2019s degree in marketing, journalism, advertising, or a related field plus two (2) years of project management experience working with Google Suite (Gmail, Docs, Drive, Sheets, etc. and project management software. Your experience must demonstrate: High energy, self-motivation with a strong work ethic Strong attention to detail Superior communication and leadership skills Superb presentation, persuasion, and project management skills Exemplary organizational skills and the ability to work effectively under pressure, handling multiple projects and tight deadlines Ability to proactively and strategically make decisions when the direction of next steps is unclear or when making a judgment call is necessary Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to work in a collaborative team environment A self-starter who is solutions-oriented and resourceful Preferred Qualifications We would prefer to see experience that includes: Managing a team Managing day-to-day operations of an office Working with a production or creative team Experience in higher education Professional experience in print production, commercial printing, publishing, marketing, or a related field. Coordinating professional print projects from concept through final production is highly desirable. Demonstrated familiarity with print production processes, print specifications, vendor management, and industry terminology. Required Licenses/Certifications Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Office setting Sometimes outdoor setting Travel Required No Physical Requirements Light work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF207 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2782 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2778": {"title": "Strategic Growth Specialist for Enrollment &amp; Market Expansion", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Strategic Growth Specialist for Enrollment &amp; Market Expansion Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Strategic Growth Specialist for Enrollment & Market Expansion Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Position Details Position Information Position Title Strategic Growth Specialist for Enrollment & Market Expansion Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division Enrollment Management Department Admissions Office Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary Doane University is a historic liberal arts college with campuses in Crete and Lincoln, Nebraska, and we are looking for a builder to help shape our future. Two positions are available, one reporting to the Director of Student Recruitment in the Office of Admission on the Crete Campus and one reporting to the Director of Student Recruitment in Enrollment Services on the Lincoln Campus. As a Strategic Growth Specialist, you play a key role in driving institutional sustainability by identifying new student markets and actively executing recruitment strategies to fill them. Moving beyond traditional athletics and performing arts streams, this role requires proactive strategy and innovative thinking to uncover underrepresented student segments, establish new sourcing pipelines, and directly recruit prospects. The ideal candidate will leverage market data to locate new student streams while acting as a compelling brand ambassador who can articulate and sell the immense value of a liberal arts education. View full job description Success Metrics Growth in enrollment for non-athletic/non-performing arts programs Increased diversity of student populations (geographic, socioeconomic, academic interests) Improved inquiry-to-enrollment conversion rates Expansion of new recruitment channels and partnerships Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. FLSA Salaried (Exempt) Salary $53,000 - $58,000 Minimum Required Qualifications Requires a bachelor\u2019s degree plus at least 3 years of experience: Independently uncovering and actively recruiting new pipelines Successfully converting passive prospects into active applicants Using data to target and capture underrepresented audience segments Building high-trust partnerships with community stakeholders Your experience must demonstrate a proven ability to: Execute strategic plans using innovative methods Use market research and data analysis to achieve goals Communicate through stories that resonate with the target audience Strong relationship-building and partnership development Effective project management and execution Adaptability in resource-constrained environments Preferred Qualifications We would also prefer to see: A master\u2019s degree with emphasis in higher education, business, marketing, or a related field 3-5 years of successful student recruitment in a liberal arts or small college environment Proven track record of leveraging a CRM (e.g., Slate, Salesforce) to manage recruitment funnels, track outreach metrics, and optimize applicant pipelines. Demonstrated ability to translate demographic and higher education enrollment trends into actionable outreach strategies. Required Licenses/Certifications Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Mobility and flexibility to conduct targeted field recruitment, requiring travel to tap into newly identified geographic territories and demographic hubs. Must be willing to connect with prospective students outside standard office hours. Travel Required Yes Physical Requirements Sedentary work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF195 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2662 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Is the salary or salary range listed in the job posting acceptable to you? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2777": {"title": "Associate Director of Communications and Media Relations", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Associate Director of Communications and Media Relations Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Associate Director of Communications and Media Relations Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Apply with a cover letter, resume, and a portfolio. Position Details Position Information Position Title Associate Director of Communications and Media Relations Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division Enrollment Management Department Office of Strategic Marketing Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary The Associate Director of Communications and Media Relations at Doane University is a key leadership role within the Office of Strategic Marketing. This position serves as a lead writer and editorial resource for the University, developing high-quality content for a variety of audiences and platforms while helping ensure a consistent institutional voice. The Associate Director will coordinate and provide editorial direction to the marketing team, freelance, contract, or other contributing writers to ensure content is accurate, engaging, on-brand, and aligned with University priorities. This position is also responsible for managing all news and public relations activities for the university, including overseeing internal monthly newsletters and collaborating with the content team to maximize positive news coverage. The associate director also plays a critical role in mitigating any sensitive media issues to ensure that Doane University is portrayed in the best possible light. Additionally, this position handles event publicity coverage and coordinates media/press events. The Associate Director of Communications and Media Relations supervises the copywriter and digital and social media specialist and reports directly to the Director of Marketing. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. FLSA Salaried (Exempt) Salary Commensuarate with experience Minimum Required Qualifications Requires a Bachelor\u2019s degree in communications, public relations, journalism, or a related field, plus at least four (4) years of progressively responsible experience in communications, public relations, or media relations. Experience must include: Crisis communications and managing sensitive media issues. Supervising staff and managing projects from conception to completion. Professional writing, editing, and storytelling across multiple formats and audiences. Success in managing media relations and securing positive media coverage. The successful candidate must be able to demonstrate: Excellent writing and editing skills, with the ability to craft press releases (AP Style). Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to build relationships and work collaboratively with diverse stakeholders. Proficiency in using various media channels and tools to disseminate information effectively. Ability to work under pressure, meet deadlines, and adapt to changing priorities. Excellent time management skills. Ability to manage multiple projects at one time. Ability to collaborate with the public, students, faculty, staff, and communities Doane serves. Technical proficiency with camera settings, lighting, and composition. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree Knowledge of higher education and/or nonprofit environments is desirable. Knowledge of Google Analytics is desirable. Knowledge of communication tools to assess media and content performance. Required Licenses/Certifications Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel between campuses is required along with flexibility for occasional travel to specific locations for photo shoots, video shoots and/or other content creation activities. Travel Required Yes Physical Requirements Sedentary work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF206 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Apply with a cover letter, resume, and a portfolio. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2776 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Portfolio Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2768": {"title": "Online Adjunct Faculty - School of Mathematics, Analytics, Computing, and Engineering and Open Learning Academy.", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Online Adjunct Faculty - School of Mathematics, Analytics, Computing, and Engineering and Open Learning Academy. Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Online Adjunct Faculty - School of Mathematics, Analytics, Computing, and Engineering and Open Learning Academy. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and transcripts (unofficial transcripts accepted for the application). Due to this is an ongoing job advertisement, only applicants selected for interviews will be contacted; turn-down notices will not be provided. Position Details Position Information Position Title Online Adjunct Faculty - School of Mathematics, Analytics, Computing, and Engineering and Open Learning Academy. Unit Extended Learning Opportunities Job Location Remote/Hybrid Option Description of Work Doane University, a nationally recognized liberal arts and sciences university in Nebraska, invites applications for an Online Adjunct Faculty position in the School of Mathematics, Analytics, Computing & Engineering and the Open Learning Academy. Doane University\u2019s Open Learning Academy is seeking adjunct faculty for the following course topics: Introductory Physics I and II and General Physics I and II. The Open Learning Academy offers rigorous 5-, 8-, and 16-week courses online to students across the nation. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. Minimum Required Qualifications Masters degree Official transcripts will be required at the time of hire as a condition of employment. Preferred Qualifications Terminal degree Priority will be given to candidates with online teaching experience. Required Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Online Travel Required No Background Check Required Yes Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC067 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and transcripts (unofficial transcripts accepted for the application). Due to this is an ongoing job advertisement, only applicants selected for interviews will be contacted; turn-down notices will not be provided. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2767 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Philosophy Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Optional Documents Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2764": {"title": "Student Recruitment Specialist", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Student Recruitment Specialist Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Student Recruitment Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Position Details Position Information Position Title Student Recruitment Specialist Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division Enrollment Management Department Admissions Office Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary Doane University is looking for a dynamic Student Recruitment Specialist to help prospective students and their families seamlessly navigate their journey from first inquiry to their very first day on campus. The Recruitment Specialist is responsible for effectively managing the recruitment of prospective students in a specialized area. The position facilitates a positive student experience from the initial inquiry by providing guidance with the admissions/ enrollment process and ensuring a smooth transition into the university. You will also communicate important University information about policies, procedures, programs, and student life in engaging, student-focused presentations. As a recruiter, you are involved with special events, both on-campus and off-campus, and daily interaction with various campus partners and the public. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. FLSA Salaried (Exempt) Salary Minimum $43,000 Minimum Required Qualifications Requires a bachelor\u2019s degree plus experience in sales, recruiting, or similar experience. Experience must include effective use of Salesforce or a similar customer relationship management tool. The successful candidate must demonstrate: Willingness and ability to travel. Friendly, professional sales attitude and demonstrated ability to influence. A consultative, solution-based soft sales approach to guide students through Doane University\u2019s application and admission processes. Outreach and networking skills for working with campus and community partners. Excellent verbal and written communication skills and the ability to establish relationships using a variety of communication channels. Ability to stay organized in a fast-paced environment and remain student-centered and responsive. A desire to represent Doane University and a passion for lifelong learning and guiding people to their next level of education. Preferred Qualifications Required Licenses/Certifications A valid driver\u2019s license and a driving record acceptable to the university\u2019s automobile insurance provider. Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Flexibility is required to communicate with prospective students outside standard office hours. Travel Required Yes Physical Requirements Light work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF205 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2763 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2761": {"title": "Fine and Performing Arts Event and Recruitment Specialist", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Fine and Performing Arts Event and Recruitment Specialist Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Ab