ired Qualifications Requires a high school diploma or equivalent and one year of experience planning, coordinating, and executing events. The successful applicant must be able to demonstrate: Excellent interpersonal skills Creative thinking and problem-solving skills Excellent organizational skills; ability to effectively manage multiple tasks at the same time Highly detail-oriented and accurate Excellent interpersonal skills Ability to work independently and self-initiate projects Comfortable learning new computer software and technology skills Strong writing and proofreading skills Preferred Qualifications A bachelor\u2019s degree and a background in fine arts are preferred. Preferred software proficiency: MS Word, Excel, Canva, Google Drive, Dropbox, Gmail, and Google Surveys. Required Licenses/Certifications Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Occasional evenings and weekends are required, with advance notice of such commitments given. Travel Required Yes Physical Requirements Sedentary work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF204 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2757 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2747": {"title": "Financial Aid Counselor", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Financial Aid Counselor Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Financial Aid Counselor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Position Details Position Information Position Title Financial Aid Counselor Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division Enrollment Management Department Financial Aid Office Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary Doane University , a liberal arts university in Crete, Nebraska, is hiring a Financial Aid Counselor to provide excellent customer service and guidance to students and their families. Don\u2019t let a lack of financial aid experience stop you from applying! While a background in financial aid is a plus, it is not mandatory. Your desire to help others succeed and the ability to show respect for each person\u2019s situation is far more important to us. We provide thorough training to ensure your success in providing assistance with all aspects of financial aid, including determining eligibility, clarifying policies, managing the loan processes, and providing information on financing options. View full job description Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. FLSA Hourly (Non-exempt) Salary $18.50 - $22.00 Minimum Required Qualifications Requires an associate\u2019s degree and two (2) years of experience in a highly regulated field that includes managing deadlines, maintaining detailed, accurate records, and ensuring confidentiality and compliance; customer service experience that includes de-escalation and problem-solving; effective verbal and written communication with internal partners and external customers. Applicants must be able to demonstrate: Genuine desire to help others succeed Commitment to showing respect for each person\u2019s situation. The ability to explain complex processes with confidence and empathy. A track record of follow-through and personal accountability. Preferred Qualifications A bachelor\u2019s degree and experience with financial aid in higher education are preferred. Experience that demonstrates the following is a plus: Collaboration across departments or functional offices. Compliance with the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act ( FERPA ). Successful use of technology to determine student eligibility and originate a financial aid award. Able to explain, in lay terms, available types of financial aid, scholarships, and general student eligibility criteria. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with diverse families. Required Licenses/Certifications Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Occasional travel between Lincoln and Crete Campuses Travel Required No Physical Requirements Sedentary work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF201 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2745 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Is the salary or salary range listed in the job posting acceptable to you? Yes No * Please describe any previous experience you have working in a customer service enviornment (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2744": {"title": "Online Adjunct Faculty - School of Natural and Life Sciences and Open Learning Academy.", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Online Adjunct Faculty - School of Natural and Life Sciences and Open Learning Academy. Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Online Adjunct Faculty - School of Natural and Life Sciences and Open Learning Academy. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and transcripts (unofficial transcripts accepted for the application). Due to this being an ongoing job advertisement, only applicants selected for interviews will be contacted; turn-down notices will not be provided. Position Details Position Information Position Title Online Adjunct Faculty - School of Natural and Life Sciences and Open Learning Academy. Unit Extended Learning Opportunities Job Location Remote/Hybrid Option Description of Work Doane University, a nationally recognized liberal arts and sciences university in Nebraska, invites applications for an Online Adjunct Faculty position for the School of Natural and Life Sciences and Open Learning Academy. Doane University\u2019s Open Learning Academy is seeking adjunct faculty for the following course topics: Organic Chemistry I and II and Biochemistry. The Open Learning Academy offers rigorous 5-, 8-, and 16-week courses online to students across the nation. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. Minimum Required Qualifications Masters degree Official transcripts will be required at the time of hire as a condition of employment. Preferred Qualifications Terminal degree Priority will be given to candidates with online teaching experience. Required Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel Required No Background Check Required Yes Outdoor Exposure Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC066 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and transcripts (unofficial transcripts accepted for the application). Due to this being an ongoing job advertisement, only applicants selected for interviews will be contacted; turn-down notices will not be provided. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2743 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2739": {"title": "Administrative Assistant for the College of Business, Humanities, &amp; Technology", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Administrative Assistant for the College of Business, Humanities, &amp; Technology Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Administrative Assistant for the College of Business, Humanities, & Technology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Position Details Position Information Position Title Administrative Assistant for the College of Business, Humanities, & Technology Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division College of Business Department College of Business Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary Under the direction of the Operations Manager for the College of Business, Humanities, & Technology, provide administrative support for the faculty and staff in the College in a fast-paced, collaborative environment. View full job description Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. FLSA Hourly (Non-exempt) Salary Hourly: $16.79 - $17.66 Minimum Required Qualifications Requires a bachelor\u2019s degree plus one year of experience in a collaborative office environment. Experience should demonstrate: Knowledge of basic office management systems and procedures Knowledge of MS Office products Knowledge of Google Workspace and project management software Ability to use typical office equipment Demonstrated interpersonal skills and customer service focus Accurate data entry and ability to transfer data from hard copy to digital databases Organizational skills and the ability to multitask Ability to set up Zoom or Google Meet video conferencing for meetings with Doane University divisions Preferred Qualifications Understanding of higher education processes Required Licenses/Certifications Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Occasional weekend or evening work for campus events is expected. Travel Required No Physical Requirements Light work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF193 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2656 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Is the salary or salary range listed in the job posting acceptable to you? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2738": {"title": "Cardinal Community Learning Centers (CCLC) After School Program (Crete Pubic Schools)", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Cardinal Community Learning Centers (CCLC) After School Program (Crete Pubic Schools) Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Cardinal Community Learning Centers (CCLC) After School Program (Crete Pubic Schools) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Cardinal Community Learning Centers (CCLC) After School Program (Crete Pubic Schools) Department Financial Aid Office Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Supervisor Reports to: CCLC Site Coordinator and Director Purpose of Job Crete Public Schools is seeking applications for CCLC Staff. This is a part-time position within the after-school program. Training is provided. This position is considered open until filled. Hourly Pay is based on related job experience. General Description and Duties Essential Functions: Supervise groups of students attending the after-school program Develop and lead club activities (i.e., arts, science, technology, sports) Clean up at the end of the daily program Assist in serving snack and dinner Other Responsibilities: Interest in building and engaging in positive relationships with students through a variety of activities Highly motivated to help students grow academically and personally A role model for kindness and a positive attitude Responsible and dependable A willingness to be flexible Organized As assigned by the supervisor Special Skills or Knowledge Required Essential Requirements: Satisfactory completion of a criminal background & NE Central Registry check You must qualify for the Federal Work Study Program and be able to work off-campus Experience supervising children is preferred Total Weekly Hours Required Flexible Physical Demands Environment: Inside and Outside Mental Demands: Ability to work under pressure and to meet timelines The ability to perform the following identified physical requirements: Physical Requirements CCLC Posting Detail Information Posting Number STU169 Number of Vacancies Multiple Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Review Start Date Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2735 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current Doane University student? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2722": {"title": "Assistant Professor of History", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Assistant Professor of History Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Assistant Professor of History Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin on October 15, and the search will continue until the position is filled. Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial accepted for applications). You will be asked for contact information for three references on the application form. Official transcripts of graduate degrees or a graduate degree in progress will be required as a condition of employment. Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor of History Unit History Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Description of Work Doane University, a nationally recognized liberal arts and sciences university in Crete, Nebraska, invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of History starting in the 2027-2028 academic year. This position begins August 16, 2027. Responsibilities include teaching 12 credit hours of on-ground undergraduate courses each semester. The position may also teach select courses online, subject to the needs of the institution. The department is seeking a generalist with the ability to teach World and European history courses. The area of specialization is open. This position will be responsible for introductory courses in world history and advanced courses with a focus on topics such as the history of the ancient world, military history, and country-specific, regional, or broader world history. Candidates may develop courses in their area of expertise as well. The opportunity to teach the program\u2019s gateway and capstone courses, Introduction to Historical Methods and the Writing and Research Seminar, is also possible. During the Fall semester, the position has the opportunity to develop a course in Doane\u2019s LAR 101 First Year Seminar program, with the topic to be chosen by the faculty member. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. Minimum Required Qualifications Qualifications: Ph.D. or Advanced ABD in History. A commitment to teaching in an undergraduate liberal arts university is expected among strong candidates. A commitment to engage in scholarly and service activities, including academic advising, is expected among strong candidates as well. Preferred Qualifications A background in Museum or Archival Studies is desirable. Required Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel Required No Background Check Required Yes Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC065 Desired Start Date 08/16/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date 10/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Review of applications will begin on October 15, and the search will continue until the position is filled. Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial accepted for applications). You will be asked for contact information for three references on the application form. Official transcripts of graduate degrees or a graduate degree in progress will be required as a condition of employment. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2720 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2719": {"title": "Talent Acquisition Partner", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Talent Acquisition Partner Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Talent Acquisition Partner Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Position Details Position Information Position Title Talent Acquisition Partner Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division University President Department Human Resources Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary The Talent Acquisition Partner serves as Doane University\u2019s lead recruiter and talent ambassador, proactively identifying, attracting, and hiring exceptional employees who advance the University\u2019s mission. Success in this position requires an individual who enjoys meeting new people, confidently initiates conversations with strangers, and views recruiting as relationship building rather than simply filling vacancies. This position actively seeks and develops relationships with talented professionals, including passive candidates who may not be actively seeking new opportunities. Through strategic sourcing, networking, social media, direct outreach, and relationship building, the Talent Acquisition Partner creates robust candidate pipelines that support the University\u2019s long-term workforce needs. This position partners closely with hiring managers throughout the recruitment and onboarding process, serving as a trusted advisor on hiring strategies, candidate evaluation, interview best practices, and successful employee integration. The Talent Acquisition Partner also supports general HR operations and special projects while maintaining exceptional customer service for employees across the University. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. FLSA Salaried (Exempt) Salary $50,600 - $61,000 Minimum Required Qualifications Requires a bachelor\u2019s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Communications, Marketing, or a related field (or equivalent experience) plus two years of progressively responsible recruiting or talent acquisition experience that includes: Successful sourcing of passive candidates through networking, social media, direct outreach, and relationship-building strategies using phone calls, email, LinkedIn, and other networking platforms. Experience managing multiple recruitment processes simultaneously. Success in this role requires the following expertise: Talent Acquisition Demonstrated ability to proactively identify, source, and recruit qualified candidates. Ability to develop relationships with passive candidates who are not actively seeking employment. Ability to build and maintain talent pipelines for current and future hiring needs. Strong interviewing and candidate assessment skills. Ability to develop creative sourcing strategies for difficult-to-fill positions. Communication Exceptional interpersonal and relationship-building skills. Confident and professional telephone presence. Outstanding written and verbal communication skills. Ability to comfortably initiate conversations with individuals at all organizational levels. Ability to represent Doane University with enthusiasm, professionalism, and authenticity. Organization Ability to manage numerous searches simultaneously while maintaining exceptional attention to detail. Strong project management and organizational skills. Ability to prioritize changing workloads in a fast-paced environment. Human Resources Working knowledge of employment laws and recruitment compliance. Ability to maintain confidential information. Ability to coach hiring managers throughout the recruitment process. Proficiency with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace and HR information systems. Preferred Qualifications Preferred Education Master\u2019s degree Preferred Experience Experience in an HR Generalist role Experience using an applicant tracking system ( ATS ) Experience in a higher education setting Helpful but not required Boolean search techniques. LinkedIn Recruiter. Employment branding. Recruitment analytics and metrics. Higher education hiring practices. Behavioral interviewing. Diversity recruitment strategies. Required Licenses/Certifications Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Occasional travel between the Lincoln and Crete campuses \u2013 primary work site is the Crete campus Travel Required No Physical Requirements Sedentary work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF198 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date 08/17/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2718 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Is the salary or salary range listed in the job posting acceptable to you? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2714": {"title": "Senior Creative Manager", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Senior Creative Manager Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Senior Creative Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Position Details Position Information Position Title Senior Creative Manager Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division Enrollment Management Department Office of Strategic Marketing Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary Doane University is hiring a Senior Creative Manager who is an integral part of the Office of Strategic Marketing ( OSM ). The position reports to the Director of Marketing and manages Doane\u2019s overall brand, ensuring consistency and accuracy across all media/outlets. Primarily, this position will develop and maintain the Doane brand, develop video creative, participate in strategic planning, and design and develop marketing and advertising collateral pieces based on established brand and design standards and desired objectives. In addition, this position approves/guides the design process of externally created materials. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. FLSA Salaried (Exempt) Salary $52,221 - $57,222 Minimum Required Qualifications Requires a bachelor\u2019s degree plus three years of progressively responsible design experience in: Creating marketing/advertising campaigns \u2014 from developing the vision and messaging platform to overseeing production on time and within budget Creating integrated content across all marketing channels: digital, social media, paid media, mobile, offline, and print Developing successful concepts Working with Adobe Creative Suite programs Digital asset management software Experience must demonstrate: Comprehensive knowledge of paper, inks, prepress processes (including bleeds, separations, PDFs, etc.), and understanding of print production (monotone to four-color printing, spot colors, coatings, etc.). Comprehensive knowledge of designing for digital mediums (websites, applications, emails, etc.) and associated processes ( RGB vs. CMYK , resolution, aspect ratios, etc.). Support video creative to include storyboard, preproduction, video editing, and post-production. Spearhead and manage content strategy for projects, harnessing brand design, copy, art and digital technology. High proficiency in Adobe Creative Suite apps, Microsoft products and other design tools. Proficient in both Mac and Windows environments. Superior communication and leadership skills. Excellent ability to establish and maintain good working relationships with colleagues and vendors. Strong organizational skills and the ability to work effectively under pressure, handling multiple projects and tight deadlines. Strengths in creative typography, corporate branding and application of branding/visual standards. High energy, self-motivated with a strong work ethic. Strong attention to detail. Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to work within a team environment. Collaborate with the team in developing marketing creative, analyzing results, and identifying opportunities. Expertise in developing marketing creative that translate objectives across business units into clear and motivating creative strategies Skilled at prioritizing work and resources across engagements, based on short- and long-term needs, and developing schedules by collaborating with the OSM team. Ability to review and approve art and copy developed by the team, ensuring that deliverables address marketing goals and challenges effectively. Skilled at producing fresh, innovative work that translates complex ideas into compelling print materials and digital experiences for audiences. Preferred Qualifications A master\u2019s degree is preferred as well as: Experience leading other designers/students Experience as a copywriter, graphic designer or production artist Experience in project management, with a focus on creative direction Experience in video creative Required Licenses/Certifications Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Availability outside of typical work hours due to University events is required. Travel Required No Physical Requirements Sedentary work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF190 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2666 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Is the salary or salary range listed in the job posting acceptable to you? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Portfolio Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2713": {"title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Communication", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Visiting Assistant Professor of Communication Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Visiting Assistant Professor of Communication Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial transcripts accepted for applications). You will be asked for contact information for three references on the application form. Official transcripts of graduate degrees, or a graduate degree in progress, will be required as a condition of employment. Review of applications will begin on July 15, and the search will continue until the position is filled. Position Details Position Information Position Title Visiting Assistant Professor of Communication Unit College of Arts & Sciences Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Description of Work Doane University, a nationally recognized liberal arts and sciences university in Crete, Nebraska, invites applications for a one-year Visiting Assistant Professor of Communication for the 2026-2027 academic year. This position begins August 10, 2026. Responsibilities include teaching 9 to 12 credit hours of on-ground undergraduate courses each semester. Courses to be taught could include Fundamentals of Communication, Writing for Social Media, Basic News Writing and Reporting, and/or other courses in Communication or the Doane Core. While teaching is the primary responsibility of this position, the successful candidate may also participate in service activities and assume limited administrative responsibilities, depending on the needs of the university and the candidate\u2019s experience and interests. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. Minimum Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Communication or related field. A commitment to teaching in an undergraduate liberal arts university is expected from strong candidates. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. or Advanced ABD in Communication or related field Required Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel Required No Background Check Required Yes Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC062 Desired Start Date 08/10/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date 07/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial transcripts accepted for applications). You will be asked for contact information for three references on the application form. Official transcripts of graduate degrees, or a graduate degree in progress, will be required as a condition of employment. Review of applications will begin on July 15, and the search will continue until the position is filled. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2694 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2712": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Engineering", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Assistant Professor of Engineering Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Assistant Professor of Engineering Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin on October 12th, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial transcripts accepted for applications). Official transcripts of degree or degree in progress will be required as a condition for employment. For further inquiries on the position, please email academicaffairs@doane.edu Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Engineering Unit Engineering & Physics Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Description of Work Doane University, a liberal arts university with campuses in Crete and Lincoln and an Omaha Location, invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Engineering with an anticipated start date of August 2027. The selected candidate will join the growing Engineering & Physics department, which offers an ABET -accredited Bachelor\u2019s degree program in Engineering with specializations in mechanical, civil, electrical, and integrated engineering. Anticipated responsibilities include teaching 24 credit hours per year, supervising engineering design projects, engaging undergraduate students in research, advising majors, and participating actively in the life of the department and university. Open to all engineering disciplines, although preference will be given to mechanical, civil, electrical, or interdisciplinary engineering candidates that would complement the expertise and talent pool of the current faculty. The ideal candidate will be able to teach core engineering courses required of all engineering majors, physics courses, and emphasis area courses within the candidate\u2019s discipline. Candidates with demonstrated teaching and industry experience are particularly encouraged to apply. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. Minimum Required Qualifications PhD preferred, but ABD or professional licensure will be considered for appointment as Visiting Assistant Professor or Assistant Professor of Practice At least one degree (undergraduate or graduate) in engineering from an ABET -accredited program Experience working in interdisciplinary engineering environments and engaging in fundamental engineering learning experiences Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates who have experience in an active learning and teaching environment, value interdisciplinary studies, are committed to teaching a diverse population of students, including students with different perspectives, and are responsive to student needs. Required Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel Required No Background Check Required Yes Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC064 Desired Start Date 08/09/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date 10/12/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Review of applications will begin on October 12th, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial transcripts accepted for applications). Official transcripts of degree or degree in progress will be required as a condition for employment. For further inquiries on the position, please email academicaffairs@doane.edu Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2700 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2711": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Management", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Assistant or Associate Professor of Management Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Assistant or Associate Professor of Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For further inquiries on the position, please email Sara Simonsen, Operations Manager of the College of Business, Humanities, and Technology, sara.simonsen@doane.edu . Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial accepted for applications). You will be asked for contact information for three references on the application form. Official transcript of graduate degrees or graduate degree in progress will be required as a condition of employment. Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Management Unit College of Business Job Location Crete, NE & Lincoln, NE Description of Work The School of Business and Leadership ( SBL ) at Doane University is seeking applicants for a full-time tenure-track faculty position as an Assistant or Associate Professor of Management. The SBL at Doane University is ACBSP -accredited and serves both undergraduate and graduate students at campuses located in Crete and Lincoln, Nebraska. The SBL provides a highly collaborative and collegial environment that is very supportive of teaching, scholarship activities, and faculty development. Responsibilities will include teaching a total of up to 24 credit hours per academic year across a variety of management courses. Course modality could include both online and in-person sections. Course location could include both Crete residential campus and Lincoln non-residential campus, teaching both undergraduate and graduate students. We have a strong interest in faculty with expertise in one or more areas, including strategy, entrepreneurship, human resources, change management, and project management. The anticipated start date for the position is August 2027. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the university. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. Minimum Required Qualifications Ph.D. or DBA in Management earned or in progress Academically qualified to meet ACBSP accreditation standards Successful experience as an instructor in management Commitment to ongoing professional activity and scholarship Candidates must have knowledge of methods to effectively instruct, motivate, and evaluate both undergraduate and graduate students, as well as: Teach across a variety of modalities Engage in faculty scholarly and service activities Participate in continuous improvement efforts within the SBL Preferred Qualifications Relevant industry experience Undergraduate, graduate, face-to-face, and online teaching experience Required Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel between Doane campuses in Crete and Lincoln Travel Required Background Check Required Yes Outdoor Exposure Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC059 Desired Start Date 08/09/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For further inquiries on the position, please email Sara Simonsen, Operations Manager of the College of Business, Humanities, and Technology, sara.simonsen@doane.edu . Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial accepted for applications). You will be asked for contact information for three references on the application form. Official transcript of graduate degrees or graduate degree in progress will be required as a condition of employment. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2643 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2710": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Marketing", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Assistant or Associate Professor of Marketing Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Assistant or Associate Professor of Marketing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For further inquiries on the position, please email Sara Simonsen, Operations Manager of the College of Business, Humanities, and Technology, sara.simonsen@doane.edu . Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial accepted for applications). You will be asked for contact information for three references on the application form. Official transcript of graduate degrees or graduate degree in progress will be required as a condition of employment. Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Marketing Unit College of Business Job Location Crete, NE & Lincoln, NE Description of Work The School of Business and Leadership ( SBL ) at Doane University is seeking applicants for a full-time tenure-track faculty position as an Assistant or Associate Professor of Marketing. The SBL at Doane University is ACBSP -accredited and serves both undergraduate and graduate students at campuses located in Crete and Lincoln, Nebraska. The SBL provides a highly collaborative and collegial environment that is very supportive of teaching, scholarship activities, and faculty development. Responsibilities will include teaching a total of up to 24 credit hours per academic year across a variety of marketing courses. Course modality could include both online and in-person sections. Course location could include both Crete residential campus and Lincoln non-residential campus, teaching both undergraduate and graduate students. We have a strong interest in faculty with expertise in one or more areas, including digital marketing, marketing research, and marketing strategy. The anticipated start date for the position is August 2027. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the university. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. Minimum Required Qualifications Ph.D. or DBA in Marketing earned or in progress Academically qualified to meet ACBSP accreditation standards Successful experience as an instructor in marketing Commitment to ongoing professional activity and scholarship Candidates must have knowledge of methods to effectively instruct, motivate, and evaluate both undergraduate and graduate students, as well as: Teach across a variety of modalities Engage in faculty scholarly and service activities Participate in continuous improvement efforts within the SBL Preferred Qualifications Relevant industry experience Undergraduate, graduate, face-to-face, and online teaching experience Required Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel between Doane campuses in Crete and Lincoln Travel Required Background Check Required Yes Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC060 Desired Start Date 08/09/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For further inquiries on the position, please email Sara Simonsen, Operations Manager of the College of Business, Humanities, and Technology, sara.simonsen@doane.edu . Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial accepted for applications). You will be asked for contact information for three references on the application form. Official transcript of graduate degrees or graduate degree in progress will be required as a condition of employment. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2644 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2709": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Finance", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Assistant or Associate Professor of Finance Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Assistant or Associate Professor of Finance Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For further inquiries on the position, please email Sara Simonsen, Operations Manager of the College of Business, Humanities, and Technology, sara.simonsen@doane.edu . Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial accepted for applications). You will be asked for contact information for three references on the application form. Official transcript of graduate degrees or graduate degree in progress will be required as a condition of employment. Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Finance Unit College of Business Job Location Crete, NE & Lincoln, NE Description of Work The School of Business and Leadership ( SBL ) at Doane University is seeking applicants for a full-time tenure-track faculty position as an Assistant or Associate Professor of Finance. The SBL at Doane University is ACBSP -accredited and serves both undergraduate and graduate students at campuses located in Crete and Lincoln, Nebraska. The SBL provides a highly collaborative and collegial environment that is very supportive of teaching, scholarship activities, and faculty development. Responsibilities will include teaching a total of up to 24 credit hours per academic year across a variety of finance courses. Course modality could include both online and in-person sections. Course location could include both Crete residential campus and Lincoln non-residential campus, teaching both undergraduate and graduate students. We have a strong interest in faculty with expertise in one or more areas, including corporate finance, fintech, investments, financial planning, and business valuation. The anticipated start date for the position is August 2027. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the university. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. Minimum Required Qualifications Ph.D. or DBA in Finance earned or in progress Academically qualified to meet ACBSP accreditation standards Successful experience as an instructor in finance Commitment to ongoing professional activity and scholarship Candidates must have knowledge of methods to effectively instruct, motivate, and evaluate both undergraduate and graduate students, as well as: Teach across a variety of modalities Engage in faculty scholarly and service activities Participate in continuous improvement efforts within the SBL Preferred Qualifications Relevant industry experience Undergraduate, graduate, face-to-face, and online teaching experience Required Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel between Doane campuses in Crete and Lincoln Travel Required Background Check Required Yes Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC058 Desired Start Date 08/09/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For further inquiries on the position, please email Sara Simonsen, Operations Manager of the College of Business, Humanities, and Technology, sara.simonsen@doane.edu . Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial accepted for applications). You will be asked for contact information for three references on the application form. Official transcript of graduate degrees or graduate degree in progress will be required as a condition of employment. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2642 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2686": {"title": "Athletics Development Officer", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Athletics Development Officer Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Athletics Development Officer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Position Details Position Information Position Title Athletics Development Officer Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division Institutional Advancement Department Development Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary Elevate your passion for collegiate sports into a rewarding fundraising career at Doane University as our Athletics Development Officer. In this role, you have the opportunity to support the Advancement and Athletics offices in achieving their annual fundraising goals across all giving levels. This position provides hands-on experience in athletics donor relations, annual giving, event coordination, corporate sponsorships, and major gift support. If you are a motivated self-starter with a passion for collegiate athletics, this is your chance to build a career in advancement and fundraising. View full job description Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. FLSA Salaried (Exempt) Salary $57,000 - $60,000 Minimum Required Qualifications Requires a bachelor\u2019s degree in Sports Management, Communications, Business, Marketing, or a related field. Success in the role requires: Strong written and verbal communication skills Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint) Demonstrated enthusiasm for collegiate athletics Preferred Qualifications We would also like to see: Prior internship or experience in fundraising, development, sales, or athletics administration Familiarity with CRM platforms (e.g., Salesforce) Experience with event planning or volunteer coordination Required Licenses/Certifications Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Willingness to work evenings, weekends, and home athletic events as required Travel Required Yes Physical Requirements Sedentary work Outdoor Exposure Exposed to both indoor and outdoor elements Background Check Required Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF194 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2685 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Is the salary or salary range listed in the job posting acceptable to you? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2532": {"title": "Graduate Assistant - Women&#39;s Soccer", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Graduate Assistant - Women&#39;s Soccer Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Graduate Assistant - Women's Soccer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The position includes a tuition waiver of up to $5,250 per calendar year (books/fees not included) Medical, dental, and vision insurance plans are available. Position Details Position Information Position Title Graduate Assistant - Women's Soccer Job Type Part Time Division Athletics Department Soccer Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary Are you passionate about soccer and ready to start your coaching career? As a Women\u2019s Soccer Graduate Assistant Coach, you\u2019ll have the opportunity to work closely with student-athletes, assist in practice planning and skill development, and gain valuable experience in a competitive collegiate environment. If you\u2019re looking to enhance your coaching skills while earning your graduate degree, this role offers the ideal balance of hands-on experience and academic growth! The Graduate Assistant Coach is responsible for working alongside the Head Coach to manage the women\u2019s soccer program and the student-athletes in the best interest of Doane University and in accordance with all the rules of the NAIA and the GPAC Conference. This position starts August 3, 2026 Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the university. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. In accordance with USCIS regulations, successful applicants must be legally able to accept work in the United States. Doane is unable to sponsor applicants for work visas. FLSA Salaried (Exempt) Salary An annual $6,750 stipend is provided, reduced to $5,000 if you live on campus, which includes a single bedroom in Frees Hall and a commuter meal plan of five meals per week plus $200 Doane Dollars per semester. Minimum Required Qualifications Must qualify for acceptance into a Doane graduate program . Bachelor\u2019s degree with competition or coaching experience at the collegiate level. General knowledge of sport, including rules, techniques, and strategies. The ability to diligently and effectively recruit and retain student-athletes Ability to teach and develop student-athletes Character Requirements: Proven record of integrity, high principles, and demonstrated skill in developing and motivating student-athletes academically and athletically. Must recognize that they are always a representative of the program and must consistently demonstrate positive coaching behavior. Organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Preferred Qualifications Required Licenses/Certifications Valid driver\u2019s license and driving record acceptable to the college\u2019s automobile insurance provider and ability to obtain certification to drive a Doane full-size minivan once hired. Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Willingness to work evenings, weekends, and travel as required. Travel Required Yes Physical Requirements Light work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to outdoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF163 Desired Start Date 08/03/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date 03/02/2026 Review Start Date 03/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant The position includes a tuition waiver of up to $5,250 per calendar year (books/fees not included) Medical, dental, and vision insurance plans are available. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2472 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Please list the colleges, universities, or clubs where you competed in competitive athletics. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2090": {"title": "Doane Tiger Mascot - Thomas the Tiger", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Doane Tiger Mascot - Thomas the Tiger Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Doane Tiger Mascot - Thomas the Tiger Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Doane Tiger Mascot - Thomas the Tiger Department Campus Engagement Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Supervisor Spencer Munson 402-826-8271 spencer.munson@doane.edu Purpose of Job Provide entertainment as our mascot, Thomas, at specific campus and community events. Meet and greet students, staff, faculty and community members, and take pictures with students, faculty, staff and community members to enhance all-around Doane University mascot experience. Provide silent entertainment projecting an enthusiastic and entertaining demeanor. General Description and Duties Have an enthusiastic and high energy at all times to keep the entertainment level high Flexibility of work depends on event and agreed schedule Assist in the development, creation and execution of performances to enhance the Doane mascot experience for tiger fans Preserve the identity of the mascot without deviating from established character including: body language/mannerisms, attitude, and fan interaction Work well in a team environment Commit entirely to the assigned scheduled opportunities for \u201cThomas\u201d to appear at on-campus and off-campus events Distribute Doane University promotional items designed to help increase school spirit and attendance at events Personally interact with students/staff/faculty/community members you encounter Special Skills or Knowledge Required Warm & engaging personality A professional demeanor and image to prove compatible with Doane University professionalism Independent and self-motivated, while flexible and adaptable A clear understanding of silent communication ability while in costume Flexible work schedule Dance experience preferred Available for up to 10 hours per week Total Weekly Hours Required 3-10 hours per week, $13.50 per hour Physical Demands Posting Detail Information Posting Number STU117 Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Review Start Date Open Date 01/26/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicant Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2073 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current Doane University student? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/1862": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - College of Business", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Adjunct Faculty - College of Business Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Adjunct Faculty - College of Business Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Note - Due to this being an ongoing job advertisement, only applicants selected for interviews will be contacted; turn-down notices will not be provided. Position Details Position Information Position Title Adjunct Faculty - College of Business Unit College of Business Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Description of Work Doane University, a nationally recognized liberal arts and sciences university in Nebraska, invites applications for Adjunct Faculty in the College of Business . The newly-formed College of Business offers undergraduate programs in the following areas: Accounting, Agribusiness, Business Administration, Economics, and Leadership. We offer minors in each of these areas, as well as in Finance, Human Resource Management, Management, and Marketing. At the graduate level, we offer an MBA and a Master of Arts in Leadership. The College of Business offers classes in Crete, Lincoln, and online. Our residential campus is located in Crete, with classes offered during the day in 16-week semesters. Most students in Crete are recent high school graduates. The Lincoln campus is geared toward working adults, with classes offered one night a week in the evening during 8-week terms. Most classes meet in person, but a few meet via distance learning. We also offer asynchronous, online classes during the 8-week terms. Candidates will only be considered for academic areas that they are qualified to teach according to our accrediting bodies. For further inquiries on the position, please email daniel.bothe@doane.edu Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the university. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. In accordance with USCIS regulations, successful applicants must be legally able to accept work in the United States. Doane is unable to sponsor applicants for work visas. HOW TO APPLY : If you are interested in teaching a class offered through the College of Business, Click on \u201cApply for this Job.\" You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, and one PDF of transcripts of all graduate work in MS Word or PDF format. In your cover letter, clearly state which academic areas you are interested in teaching, as well as which locations (Crete, Lincoln) and modalities (in-person, distance learning, and online) you are willing to teach. Official transcript of terminal degree or degree in progress will be required as a condition for employment. Minimum Required Qualifications A master\u2019s degree is required. Priority will be given to candidates with teaching experience and professional business experience. Preferred Qualifications A terminal degree is preferred. Preference will be given to candidates who have experience in an active learning and teaching environment, value interdisciplinary studies, are committed to teaching to a diverse population of students, include students with different perspectives, and are responsive to student needs. Required Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel Required Background Check Required Yes Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC011 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Note \u2013 Due to this being an ongoing job advertisement, only applicants selected for interviews will be contacted; turn-down notices will not be provided. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/1161 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/1861": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty \u2013 Agribusiness Department", "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Adjunct Faculty \u2013 Agribusiness Department Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Adjunct Faculty \u2013 Agribusiness Department Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. HOW TO APPLY: If you are interested in teaching a class offered through the College of Business, Click on \u201cApply for this Job.\" You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, and one PDF of transcripts of all graduate work in MS Word or PDF format. Position Details Position Information Position Title Adjunct Faculty \u2013 Agribusiness Department Unit College of Business Job Location Remote/Hybrid Option Description of Work Doane University, a nationally recognized liberal arts and sciences university in Nebraska, invites applications for Adjunct Faculty in the Agribusiness Department of the College of Business. The Agribusiness Department offers online classes to students attending the Crete residential campus and students living remotely with different ages and work experience. The Agribusiness courses offer asynchronous, online classes during 8-week terms. Areas of need and time frames include: Agribusiness Management Introductory Agribusiness Principles Applied Agricultural Technology and Data Analysis Agribusiness Sustainability For further inquiries on these positions, please email daniel.bothe@doane.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the university. Doane University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. In accordance with USCIS regulations, successful applicants must be legally able to accept work in the United States. Doane is unable to sponsor applicants for work visas. Minimum Required Qualifications A master\u2019s degree is required. Priority will be given to candidates with online teaching experience and professional agribusiness or agricultural experience. Preferred Qualifications A terminal degree is preferred. Preference will be given to candidates who have experience in an active learning and teaching environment, value interdisciplinary studies, are committed to teaching to a diverse population of students, include students with different perspectives, and are responsive to student needs. Required Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel Required No Background Check Required Yes Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC025 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date 07/09/2024 Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant HOW TO APPLY : If you are interested in teaching a class offered through the College of Business, Click on \u201cApply for this Job.\" You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, and one PDF of transcripts of all graduate work in MS Word or PDF format. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/1594 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top \u00a9 Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}}, "rows": {"https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2789": {"school_id": 831, "posting_url": "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2789", "job_title_in_post": "Data Specialist II", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2788": {"school_id": 831, "posting_url": "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2788", "job_title_in_post": "Employer Relations Coordinator", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "12/01/2026"}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2787": {"school_id": 831, "posting_url": "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2787", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct Faculty - Communications", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "School of Communication, English, History, and Spanish Job Location Crete, NE", "area_key_words": "Communications; liberal arts university", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "01/11/2027"}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2783": {"school_id": 831, "posting_url": "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2783", "job_title_in_post": "Project Manager", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2778": {"school_id": 831, "posting_url": "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2778", "job_title_in_post": "Strategic Growth Specialist for Enrollment &amp; Market Expansion", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2777": {"school_id": 831, "posting_url": "https